{% extends "_base.txt.j2" %}
{% set kicker = "CANARY DETECTED SUPPLY DELTA" %}
{% set headline = "Canary Fire Produced Supply Imbalance" %}
{% block body %}
A canary synthetic transfer triggered a supply invariant deviation. The canary system fires
real production transfers between dedicated system agents. When the cross-frame ledger
snapshot before vs after a fire shows non-zero Δ, it indicates a correctness regression in
the transfer pipeline.

  Frame:        {{ frame }}
  Delta:        {{ delta }}
  Path:         {{ path }}
  Backend:      {{ backend }}
  Test ID:      {{ test_id }}
  Sender:       {{ sender_did }}
  Receiver:     {{ receiver_did }}
  Detected at:  {{ detected_at }}

Investigate: {{ registry_ui_url }}#/admin

CLI:
  docker exec agentvault_event_store_db psql -U postgres -d eventstore \
    -c "SELECT event_type, source_service, timestamp FROM events
        WHERE event_data::text LIKE '%{{ test_id }}%' ORDER BY timestamp"

A canary-detected delta is more actionable than the projection-based auditor: it pinpoints
the offending transfer.
{% endblock %}
